Consider the following C program:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int compute(int x) {
    static int s = 1;
    s = s + x;
    return s;
}
int main() {
    int i, total = 0;
    for (i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
        total += compute(i);
    }
    printf("%d", total);
    return 0;
}
```

The integer value printed by the above program is __________.

A main process executes a loop containing a single fork() system call exactly 4 times:

  ```c
for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
      fork();
  }
```

Assuming all fork() calls succeed, how many NEW child processes are created (excluding the original parent process)?

